<article class="ws-sheet">
<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 14th century</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 1300s: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/14th-century">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 1350 CE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 8385 4413" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 1350 CE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="5709" cy="970" r="143"/><text x="5709" y="1030" font-size="171">1</text></g><g><circle cx="6352" cy="637" r="143"/><text x="6352" y="697" font-size="171">2</text></g><g><circle cx="5054" cy="728" r="143"/><text x="5054" y="788" font-size="171">3</text></g><g><circle cx="4769" cy="1989" r="143"/><text x="4769" y="2049" font-size="171">4</text></g><g><circle cx="5815" cy="1335" r="143"/><text x="5815" y="1395" font-size="171">5</text></g><g><circle cx="5556" cy="562" r="143"/><text x="5556" y="622" font-size="171">6</text></g><g><circle cx="7559" cy="780" r="143"/><text x="7559" y="840" font-size="171">7</text></g><g><circle cx="6029" cy="1964" r="143"/><text x="6029" y="2024" font-size="171">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 1350 CE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Kingdom of France &middot; Mongol Empire &middot; Mamluk Sultanate &middot; Golden Horde &middot; Ottoman Empire &middot; Ethiopian Empire &middot; Mali Empire &middot; Grand Duchy of Lithuania</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Kulikovo</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Aljubarrota</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Bannockburn</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Crécy</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Nicopolis</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Hundred Years' War</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Muhammad bin Tughluq</li><li>Dante Alighieri</li><li>Algirdas</li><li>Petrarch</li><li>Hongwu Emperor</li><li>Ivan I of Moscow</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1328–1398</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 1296–1377</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 1288–1340</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 1290–1351</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1265–1321</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1304–1374</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 1300s, 284 recorded states were founded and 181 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Ottoman Empire, the Golden Horde and the Kingdom of France. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 14th century, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/14th-century. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 14th century</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Ottoman Empire <span>1299 CE – 1922 CE</span></li><li>Golden Horde <span>1242 CE – 1502 CE</span></li><li>Kingdom of France <span>987 CE – 1792 CE</span></li><li>Mali Empire <span>1235 CE – 1600 CE</span></li><li>Mamluk Sultanate <span>1250 CE – 1517 CE</span></li><li>Grand Duchy of Lithuania <span>1236 CE – 1795 CE</span></li><li>Mongol Empire <span>1206 CE – 1368 CE</span></li><li>Ethiopian Empire <span>1270 CE – 1974 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Battle of Bannockburn <span>1314</span></li><li>Hundred Years' War <span>1337–1453</span></li><li>Battle of Crécy <span>1346</span></li><li>Battle of Kulikovo <span>1380</span></li><li>Battle of Aljubarrota <span>1385</span></li><li>Battle of Nicopolis <span>1396</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Muhammad bin Tughluq <span>4: c. 1290–1351</span></li><li>Dante Alighieri <span>5: 1265–1321</span></li><li>Algirdas <span>2: c. 1296–1377</span></li><li>Petrarch <span>6: 1304–1374</span></li><li>Hongwu Emperor <span>1: 1328–1398</span></li><li>Ivan I of Moscow <span>3: c. 1288–1340</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
